From b2cbfa4038e998550d75dda1ebd1a55e5d1fdf20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 06:23:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vo/vulkan/win: lock presentation to the host vblank for
 display-sync feedback

Win32/Vulkan had no get_vsync. mpv does not own the swapchain and there is
no Vulkan API on Windows for past presentation timing, so display-sync ran
without feedback: a vblank physically missed by the swapchain was invisible
to vo.c, the A/V difference did not move, and neither drop_repeat nor the
display-tempo audio loop corrected it; the picture stayed one vblank off.

Pin down when a frame is shown instead of guessing it afterwards:

- A detached watcher thread waits on the real scan-out vblank of the
  window's monitor (D3DKMTWaitForVerticalBlankEvent, re-opened when the
  window changes monitors) and keeps a vblank index with a smoothed
  phase/period estimate (initial period from 30 consistent intervals, then
  phase += 0.1*err, period += 0.002*err/n, outlier rejection, restart after
  long gaps). It holds a module reference and exits through
  FreeLibraryAndExitThread, so unloading libmpv cannot remove its code.

- swap_buffers blocks until the first vblank after the present, so the VO
  advances one vblank per swap. get_vsync reports that vblank's time and
  the vblank count skipped since the previous swap. A late present lands on
  a later vblank, the reported spacing becomes 2+ periods, vo.c's skip
  detection fires and display-sync sees the slip in the A/V difference.

With vulkan-swap-mode=mailbox and swapchain-depth=1 the mapping is exact:
libplacebo's swap_buffers returns only after the frame's GPU work finished,
and mailbox latches the newest ready image at the next vblank. FIFO does not
double-wait (one image per vblank in, one per vblank out) but may show the
image a vblank later than reported.

Statistics every 10 s at -v ("vsync-lock:"): host rate, late swaps and
skipped vblanks, present offset inside the refresh cycle, wait time,
swaps without feedback, watcher wake-ups missed. Without the D3DKMT API, or
until the estimate has settled, nothing is reported and vo.c keeps its
fallback path.

MPV_VSYNC_LOCK selects how much of the lock runs, to isolate its effects
inside one build: 0 off, 1 watcher thread only, 2 watcher + swap_buffers
pacing without feedback, 3 (default) watcher + pacing + feedback,
4 watcher + pre-render pacing without feedback, 5 watcher + pre-render
pacing + feedback, 7 present phase lock + feedback, 8 present phase lock
of the present only + feedback. The chosen mode is logged once at info level
("vsync-lock: MPV_VSYNC_LOCK=").

Pre-render pacing moves the wait from the end of swap_buffers to the start
of the next frame (the check_visible hook at the top of draw_frame, before
the image is acquired). vo.c wakes the core right before draw_frame, so with
the wait at the end of swap_buffers the core's filter chain (e.g. GPU
upscaler inference) and the VO's rendering start together right after every
vblank; with the wait before rendering the core is woken right after the
present instead. Frames are rendered, presented and reported at the same
vblanks in both variants.

Mode 7 is a port of shadPS4's VsyncLock with its AccurateTimer (the
drop-missed-intervals variant), for vulkan-swap-mode=mailbox. Nothing waits
for the vblank itself: a timer before each frame (check_visible, top of
draw_frame) paces the VO, and its interval is trimmed so that the present
lands MPV_VSYNC_LOCK_MARGIN_MS (1 - 50, default 6) before the host vblank.
Target phase, gain (0.1), slew limits (0.5% acquiring, 500 ppm locked),
lock hysteresis (0.5 ms for 60 frames / 2 ms for 30 frames), the 60-sample
estimate requirement and the timer arithmetic follow shadPS4; the sleep uses
a high-resolution waitable timer. shadPS4 takes the phase at the top of its
present loop, where Present() follows right away; here rendering and
uploading take a sizeable and variable part of the cycle before the
present, so the phase is taken at the present.

Reporting for mode 7 follows mailbox semantics: a present that misses the
vblank it was meant for is normally replaced by the next frame (the previous
image is repeated and this one dropped, which leaves the video position
unchanged), so it is reported at the expected vblank; if the next frame
shows that it was not replaced, the next report carries the real position.
Intervals dropped by the timer (slots without a new image) are reported as
skipped vblanks. Statistics every 10 s also give the lock state and the
phase error ("vsync-lock: host ... Hz, locked, phase err mean ...").

Mode 8 keeps mode 7's timer and phase lock but holds back only the present,
which is what shadPS4's present thread does: its guest renders on its own and
only the flip waits for the timer. Pacing the whole VO iteration (modes 2-5
and 7) also moves the core wake-up that vo.c issues right before draw_frame,
and with it the filter chain (e.g. GPU upscaler inference), so the GPU work
of the pipeline gets interleaved differently than without the lock. In mode 8
rendering runs as without the lock and only the finished image waits for its
slot. For that, a pre_present hook (ra_ctx_params / ra_swapchain_fns) is
called right before the present: from vo_gpu_next's flip_page before
pl_swapchain_submit_frame (the rendering has already been flushed to the GPU
by pl_gpu_flush at the end of draw_frame), and from the Vulkan context's
submit_frame for vo_gpu. Contexts that do not set the hook are unaffected.
---
 video/out/gpu/context.h        |    8 +
 video/out/vo_gpu_next.c        |    2 +
 video/out/vulkan/context.c     |    9 +
 video/out/vulkan/context_win.c | 1061 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 1080 insertions(+)

diff --git a/video/out/gpu/context.h b/video/out/gpu/context.h
index 6c5d008..7c747e8 100644
--- a/video/out/gpu/context.h
+++ b/video/out/gpu/context.h
@@ -88,6 +88,9 @@ struct ra_ctx_params {
     // ra_gl_ctx_swap_buffers. Required unless you either never call that
     // function or if you override it yourself.
     void (*swap_buffers)(struct ra_ctx *ctx);
+
+    // See ra_swapchain_fns.pre_present. Optional.
+    void (*pre_present)(struct ra_ctx *ctx);
 };
 
 // Extra struct for the swapchain-related functions so they can be easily
@@ -130,6 +133,11 @@ struct ra_swapchain_fns {
     // swapchains smart enough to do something with it.
     bool (*submit_frame)(struct ra_swapchain *sw, const struct vo_frame *frame);
 
+    // Called right before a rendered frame is presented, after its rendering
+    // commands have been flushed to the GPU. Lets the context decide when the
+    // present happens without holding back the rendering. Optional.
+    void (*pre_present)(struct ra_swapchain *sw);
+
     // Performs a buffer swap. This blocks for as long as necessary to meet
     // params.swapchain_depth, or until the next vblank (for vsynced contexts)
     void (*swap_buffers)(struct ra_swapchain *sw);
diff --git a/video/out/vo_gpu_next.c b/video/out/vo_gpu_next.c
index 308a9fb..ea27156 100644
--- a/video/out/vo_gpu_next.c
+++ b/video/out/vo_gpu_next.c
@@ -1514,6 +1514,8 @@ static void flip_page(struct vo *vo)
     struct ra_swapchain *sw = p->ra_ctx->swapchain;
 
     if (p->frame_pending) {
+        if (sw->fns->pre_present)
+            sw->fns->pre_present(sw);
         if (!pl_swapchain_submit_frame(p->sw))
             MP_ERR(vo, "Failed presenting frame!\n");
         p->frame_pending = false;
diff --git a/video/out/vulkan/context.c b/video/out/vulkan/context.c
index d062ea8..8c2fd81 100644
--- a/video/out/vulkan/context.c
+++ b/video/out/vulkan/context.c
@@ -522,9 +522,17 @@ static bool start_frame(struct ra_swapchain *sw, struct ra_fbo *out_fbo)
     return true;
 }
 
+static void pre_present(struct ra_swapchain *sw)
+{
+    struct priv *p = sw->priv;
+    if (p->params.pre_present)
+        p->params.pre_present(sw->ctx);
+}
+
 static bool submit_frame(struct ra_swapchain *sw, const struct vo_frame *frame)
 {
     struct priv *p = sw->priv;
+    pre_present(sw);
     return pl_swapchain_submit_frame(p->vk->swapchain);
 }
 
@@ -589,6 +597,7 @@ static const struct ra_swapchain_fns vulkan_swapchain = {
     .target_csp    = target_csp,
     .start_frame   = start_frame,
     .submit_frame  = submit_frame,
+    .pre_present   = pre_present,
     .swap_buffers  = swap_buffers,
     .get_vsync     = get_vsync,
 };
